/**
 * @page topic_audio Audio System
 * @ingroup module_audio
 * @brief Native audio capture, playback, processing, and device selection.
 *
 * The audio system owns device setup and realtime callbacks. Session code selects
 * capture/playback policy and connects the audio context to the client pipeline;
 * the network layer carries batches separately.
 *
 * @section audio_devices Devices
 *
 * Device enumeration and selection are explicit. The default device is used
 * when no index is supplied. Missing microphones are allowed when playback or a
 * non-device media source does not need capture.
 *
 * @section audio_realtime Realtime path
 *
 * Audio callbacks must remain bounded and allocation-free. They exchange samples
 * with ring buffers/pipelines; encoding, logging, network I/O, and UI updates
 * happen outside the callback. Underruns produce silence and are observable in
 * diagnostics rather than blocking the device thread.
 *
 * @section audio_platform Platforms
 *
 * PortAudio-backed native builds use the host's available backend. Browser and
 * iOS paths use their platform audio bridges. Do not document a backend as
 * guaranteed merely because it is available on one development machine.
 *
 * @see topic_client_audio
 * @see topic_mixer
 * @see topic_tui
 */
